# Build-context exclusions for soak/Dockerfile.soak ONLY.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context root's
# `.dockerignore`, which is why this lives here: the repo has no root
# `.dockerignore` and adding one would silently change the context of every
# other build anyone ever runs against this tree.
#
# The line that matters is `node_modules`. The build context is the repo root,
# which on the box that produced it is a WINDOWS checkout — `COPY . .` would
# drop Windows-native @prisma/client engines and esbuild/sharp binaries on top
# of the Linux tree `npm ci` had just installed, and the relay would fail at
# require() time with an error that reads like a Prisma schema problem. It also
# copies a multi-GB directory across for nothing.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded: e2e-evidence/, android/, tools/. They cost little
# and something in the build reading a file this list had quietly removed is a
# worse failure than a larger context.
node_modules
.next
.git

# Never bake a real secret into a soak image. The stack takes SOAK_JWT_SECRET
# from the environment at run time; .env.example is kept because it is
# documentation, not a credential.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production

# Another lane's lock file must never travel into an image.
.e2e-lock
